        "Normalization of total complexes", H("Normalization of total complexes"), Blocks(
        Paragraph(Text("Let C : Type u have Category.{v} C and Abelian C, with independent universes, and let X be bisimplicial. MOne(X) denotes the total complex with outer alternating faces and inner Moore normalization. The comparison factors as NOne(X) ≃ MOne(X) ≃ FOne(X), using the ordinary Dold–Kan normalization homotopy in each direction.")),
        Paragraph(Text("The outer homotopy-lifting construction is more general: I₁,I₂,J are arbitrary index types with shapes c₁,c₂,c, DecidableEq J and TotalComplexShape c₁ c₂ c. K,L are double complexes in C with HasTotal c, and φ,ψ : K → L. A Homotopy φ ψ in the first complex direction gives totalMapHomotopy. Its summand signs are the native ε₁ signs, and the homotopy vanishes away from c.Rel j′ j. The inner-direction version uses the corresponding homotopy in HomologicalComplex C c₁ and flips the double complexes.")),
        Paragraph(Text("The native totalFlipIso multiplies a natural-number bidegree (p,q) summand by (-1)^(p*q). Its naturality identifies the actual total map with the conjugate of the flipped total map. This transfers the inner normalization homotopy without altering either differential sign. The category and normalization suppliers are the pinned implementations.")),
